WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.680 --> 00:00:07.940
A latch tool, also called a Tappet tool,
is just a machine needle with a handle.

2
00:00:07.970 --> 00:00:13.060
It has a number of different
uses to manually form stitches.

3
00:00:13.090 --> 00:00:15.500
Most commonly, it's used to reverse

4
00:00:15.530 --> 00:00:19.420
stitches, turning knit
stitches into Purl stitches.

5
00:00:19.450 --> 00:00:25.800
Notice how the Purl bump is showing
against the knit stitches in this example.

6
00:00:26.120 --> 00:00:28.020
To reform an existing stitch,

7
00:00:28.050 --> 00:00:34.460
push the tool into a stitch below the one
that's currently in work on a needle.

8
00:00:34.490 --> 00:00:37.900
Drop the stitch off
the needle and un-ravel it.

9
00:00:37.930 --> 00:00:41.520
Forming a ladder.

10
00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:48.700
Use the tool to pick up each ladder,
forming new stitches.

11
00:00:48.730 --> 00:00:53.300
To create a column of reformed
stitches, drop a single stitch.

12
00:00:53.330 --> 00:00:58.560
Pick up each ladder, forming new stitches.

13
00:01:03.640 --> 00:01:08.180
When the last strand has been knit,
rehang the stitch on the needle.

14
00:01:08.210 --> 00:01:12.880
Now you have a column
of reformed stitches.

15
00:01:21.280 --> 00:01:24.180
This can be done across a row

16
00:01:24.210 --> 00:01:30.660
for a turning row or a manually
formed decorative Purl row.

17
00:01:30.690 --> 00:01:34.460
Another use of the latch
tool is for binding off.

18
00:01:34.490 --> 00:01:36.240
Knit the last row of your knitting

19
00:01:36.270 --> 00:01:41.290
at the loosest tension or
manually knit a loose row.

20
00:01:41.320 --> 00:01:43.380
Slip the first stitch off the needle

21
00:01:43.410 --> 00:01:48.290
and place it on the tool
behind the latch of the tool.

22
00:01:48.320 --> 00:01:53.820
Slip the adjacent stitch to the tool
in the hook on the tool.

23
00:01:53.850 --> 00:01:57.540
Purl the second stitch through the first.

24
00:01:57.570 --> 00:02:01.020
This is called a stitch
through stitch Bindoff.

25
00:02:01.050 --> 00:02:05.420
This method is fast, but it may
not be as stretchy as you need.

26
00:02:05.450 --> 00:02:10.880
Please try other bind off
methods in addition to this one.

27
00:02:20.760 --> 00:02:25.420
Any time you use a latch tool,
remember you're positioning a needle

28
00:02:25.450 --> 00:02:29.100
in the opposite direction
of the needle on the needle bed.

29
00:02:29.130 --> 00:02:34.140
If you reform stitches,
they will be facing the opposite way.

30
00:02:34.170 --> 00:02:37.600
Think about knit and Purl stitches,
as in hand knitting.

